# The script of every c-testsuite test (msil_ctest_format.py yields one lit
# test per name of libc-free.txt, 'MSIL :: Programs/c-testsuite/<name>', and
# lit runs this file as if it were the test's own). The format gives the
# test four substitutions: %{msil_ctest_name} (the name), %{msil_ctest_tree}
# (the cached tree, c-testsuite-<ref>), %{msil_ctest_cflags} (the recon's
# flags, -std=gnu17 -w: no -ffreestanding, because several tests rely on
# main's implicit 'return 0') and %{msil_ctest_run}: %{msil_prog}, which
# builds the test through the leg's pipeline at each of its levels and runs
# it against exit0.expected (as the native oracle build), or for a
# '<name> diag <text>' entry one %{msil_prog_fail_<L>} per level, piped into
# FileCheck of the text (diag.check). The placeholders are redefined here,
# not given as substitutions of the format, which lit would apply before
# lit.cfg.py's definitions (its %{msil_srcs} would then win inside
# %{msil_prog}). Plan 5.12.9 (M23). This file is not a test itself.
# REQUIRES: msil-corpus-c-testsuite
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %{msil_corpus}/%{msil_ctest_tree}/tests/single-exec/%{msil_ctest_name}.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_cflags} = %{msil_ctest_cflags}
# REDEFINE: %{msil_expect} = %S/exit0
# RUN: %{msil_ctest_run}
